# 2026-10-28: files that carry a credential literal - never tracked

# Tooling state and other sessions' scratch files - not ours to track.
.cursor/
.netlify/
.openclaw/
.tmp-*.sh
.tmp-*.py
# Scratch DIRECTORIES too. ".tmp-*.sh"/".tmp-*.py" only match FILES, so a
# ".tmp-something/" directory was never ignored - and one of those held
# nested .git repos, which `git add .` would stage as embedded repos
# (gitlink entries) and break every clone. The canonical checker
# `git-index` now fails on that class of damage; this rule stops it
# reaching the index in the first place.
.tmp-*/
</newString>
# Media binaries: 2.2 MB of video has no place in a PUBLIC repo, and
# a binary in the tracked set is a fragment-matching risk. The deploy
# copies them from the working tree, not from git.
studex-meat/public/media/*.mp4
studex-meat/public/media/*.mp3
studex-meat/public/media/*.mov
studex-meat/public/media/*.wav

# Moved-out-of-service checkers live here, recoverable, never tracked.
.trash-*/

# One-shot scratch scripts written into ops/ by cron agents (standup probes,
# EOD sweeps). They are scratch, they are kept on disk, and they must not
# reach the PUBLIC remote - the existing '.tmp-*.py' rule does not match them
# because they carry no leading dot. Untracked 2026-10-29.
ops/tmp-*
ops/logs/
